  "request": "Compose a 90-second Raag Bhairav × heavy metal piece in the key of E (Sa = E), in teentaal at 128 BPM.  Open with Bhairav, introduce a memorable heavy riff, develop it through lead-and-riff call and response, build into a fast taan climax, and finish with a tihai landing exactly on sam. Reuse and transform one recognisable Bhairav motif so the piece sounds developed rather than assembled. End with a hard stop: the lead lands on upper Sa while guitar, bass and drums strike low Sa underneath it.  I will play the rhythm guitar live, so keep it playable on a standard six-string in E standard: anchor on the open low E, one core riff with a few variations, mostly eighth notes with only short sixteenth-note bursts."
}